INT. FLOODED ORCHARD COTTAGE - KITCHEN - NIGHT

Rain drums on a tin roof. Water has crept an inch under the door and pools on the flagstones. A single candle burns on the kitchen table, beside a black rotary phone, its cord stretched taut across the room.

DETECTIVE PERPETUA LOWRY, fifties, in a drenched mackintosh, stands with the receiver at her ear. She doesn't sit. A cup of cold tea has been on the table so long it has grown a skin.

CALLER (V.O.)
(over phone, thin, amused)
You came alone.

PERPETUA
I did.

CALLER (V.O.)
That was brave.

PERPETUA
It was cheaper than a team.

A long pause on the line. Rain. A drip from the ceiling lands in the cup.

CALLER (V.O.)
Do you know where Edmund Hale is, Detective?

PERPETUA
In a drawer at the county morgue.

CALLER (V.O.)
Then you know I didn't do it.

PERPETUA
I know you wanted me to think so.

She picks up a pencil and turns it between her fingers. She studies the pooling water. She walks, slowly, to the window and looks out at the black orchard, where bare branches thrash.

CALLER (V.O.)
Look at the third tree from the gate.

Perpetua doesn't move.

CALLER (V.O.) (CONT'D)
Go on.

She leans closer to the glass. Her breath fogs it. A dark shape hangs from the third tree, swinging in the wind. She stares. Her shoulders drop a quarter inch.

PERPETUA
(very quietly)
That's a coat.

CALLER (V.O.)
It's his coat.

PERPETUA
Where is he?

CALLER (V.O.)
Why would I tell you? You haven't asked my name.

PERPETUA
You've been calling me for six nights. I've heard you breathe. I know you've been drinking.

CALLER (V.O.)
Whisky. A decent one.

PERPETUA
Then you can say your name over a decent whisky.

A pause. The receiver crackles. When the voice returns it is lower, tired.

ROSCOE (V.O.)
(over phone)
Roscoe Hale. Edmund's brother.

Perpetua closes her eyes. The pencil snaps in her fist.

PERPETUA
You buried him in the orchard.

ROSCOE (V.O.)
I buried what was left.

PERPETUA
Why call me?

ROSCOE (V.O.)
Because someone should know where he is. And the police won't dig in the rain.

She sets the broken pencil on the table. She looks at the candle, at the cold tea, at the dark window.

PERPETUA
Roscoe. Where are you now?

ROSCOE (V.O.)
Look at the gate.

She turns. In the doorway of the kitchen, silhouetted by lightning, a man's shape is standing with a phone in his hand.

Thunder. The candle gutters out.
